(go/type Config "A Config structure configures a QUIC endpoint.\nA Config must not be modified after it has been passed to a QUIC function.\nA Config may be reused; the quic package will also not modify it.\n" (struct


    ^{:line 22 :tag (* tls/Config) :doc "TLSConfig is the endpoint's TLS configuration.\nIt must be non-nil and include at least one certificate or else set GetCertificate.\n"} TLSConfig





    ^{:line 28 :tag int64 :doc "MaxBidiRemoteStreams limits the number of simultaneous bidirectional streams\na peer may open.\nIf zero, the default value of 100 is used.\nIf negative, the limit is zero.\n"} MaxBidiRemoteStreams





    ^{:line 34 :tag int64 :doc "MaxUniRemoteStreams limits the number of simultaneous unidirectional streams\na peer may open.\nIf zero, the default value of 100 is used.\nIf negative, the limit is zero.\n"} MaxUniRemoteStreams





    ^{:line 40 :tag int64 :doc "MaxStreamReadBufferSize is the maximum amount of data sent by the peer that a\nstream will buffer for reading.\nIf zero, the default value of 1MiB is used.\nIf negative, the limit is zero.\n"} MaxStreamReadBufferSize





    ^{:line 46 :tag int64 :doc "MaxStreamWriteBufferSize is the maximum amount of data a stream will buffer for\nsending to the peer.\nIf zero, the default value of 1MiB is used.\nIf negative, the limit is zero.\n"} MaxStreamWriteBufferSize





    ^{:line 52 :tag int64 :doc "MaxConnReadBufferSize is the maximum amount of data sent by the peer that a\nconnection will buffer for reading, across all streams.\nIf zero, the default value of 1MiB is used.\nIf negative, the limit is zero.\n"} MaxConnReadBufferSize







    ^{:line 60 :tag bool :doc "RequireAddressValidation may be set to true to enable address validation\nof client connections prior to starting the handshake.\n\nEnabling this setting reduces the amount of work packets with spoofed\nsource address information can cause a server to perform,\nat the cost of increased handshake latency.\n"} RequireAddressValidation
















    ^{:line 77 :tag (array 32 byte) :doc "StatelessResetKey is used to provide stateless reset of connections.\nA restart may leave an endpoint without access to the state of\nexisting connections. Stateless reset permits an endpoint to respond\nto a packet for a connection it does not recognize.\n\nThis field should be filled with random bytes.\nThe contents should remain stable across restarts,\nto permit an endpoint to send a reset for\nconnections created before a restart.\n\nThe contents of the StatelessResetKey should not be exposed.\nAn attacker can use knowledge of this field's value to\nreset existing connections.\n\nIf this field is left as zero, stateless reset is disabled.\n"} StatelessResetKey




    ^{:line 82 :tag time/Duration :doc "HandshakeTimeout is the maximum time in which a connection handshake must complete.\nIf zero, the default of 10 seconds is used.\nIf negative, there is no handshake timeout.\n"} HandshakeTimeout







    ^{:line 90 :tag time/Duration :doc "MaxIdleTimeout is the maximum time after which an idle connection will be closed.\nIf zero, the default of 30 seconds is used.\nIf negative, idle connections are never closed.\n\nThe idle timeout for a connection is the minimum of the maximum idle timeouts\nof the endpoints.\n"} MaxIdleTimeout






    ^{:line 97 :tag time/Duration :doc "KeepAlivePeriod is the time after which a packet will be sent to keep\nan idle connection alive.\nIf zero, keep alive packets are not sent.\nIf greater than zero, the keep alive period is the smaller of KeepAlivePeriod and\nhalf the connection idle timeout.\n"} KeepAlivePeriod









    ^{:line 107 :tag (* slog/Logger) :doc "QLogLogger receives qlog events.\n\nEvents currently correspond to the definitions in draft-ietf-qlog-quic-events-03.\nThis is not the latest version of the draft, but is the latest version supported\nby common event log viewers as of the time this paragraph was written.\n\nThe qlog package contains a slog.Handler which serializes qlog events\nto a standard JSON representation.\n"} QLogLogger))




